    "body": "## Summary\n\nThe layerwise layout already reports its aggregate overhead:\n\n```\nLayerwise param layout: 199 params, 1 buckets, dp_size=60, total_param_numel=2566062080,\ntotal_buffer_numel=12582912000, total_padding=10016849920 (shard_imbalance=10016849920),\noverhead=390.4%\n```\n\nThat says a buffer is wasteful, but not which bucket or which tensor made it so. A shard is the fullest bin after packing, so one parameter larger than a balanced share forces every shard in its bucket to its size, and no rebalancing helps. Many similar parameters that merely pack poorly are a different problem with a different fix (more buckets, or a different `bucket_size`).\n\nThis adds one INFO line per bucket, next to where the padded shard size is computed:\n\n```\nLayerwise bucket 0: shard=209715200 x dp=60, real=2566062080, largest=[...]\n```\n\nIf `largest[0]` equals the shard size, the bucket is held hostage by one tensor; if the largest few are well below it, packing is the problem.\n\n- Numels rather than shapes: the function receives unnamed parameters, and a numel identifies a tensor as well as a shape here while keeping the line short.\n- One line per bucket, so log volume follows bucket count, not parameter count.\n- `chunk_params` can contain `None` (the shared-embedding path), hence the filter.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
